# The moment (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): the weather, the day, festivals, lore and where you're from, as
# chains. One remarks on the moment; the other answers as they are (moment.reply_weather, _day, _festival, _lore,
# _home: chosen by the answerer's job, home, age, means and temper); the first closes it (moment.close), in kind with
# what the answer was.
#
# Two pair memories carry the chain (two minutes: a chain's beats are chosen at once):
#   m7o  what kind of opener it was, where a reply has to know: need (cold, hungry, homeless), far (from elsewhere),
#        busy (working while others rest), pup (a pup's question), tale (lore), and for the day: market, stall, rest,
#        dawn, dusk, night, crowd, quiet, done (after a shift), dayoff. Replies keyed to it have priority, so a chain's
#        best tier always answers what was actually said.
#   m7   how the answer went, for the close: moan, glad, joke, work, poor, posh, weary, hungry, fear, boats, crowd,
#        gossip, home, local, prickly, gladgone, offer, same, snub, sorry, farre, together, tease, busy, topup,
#        pupchat, pupgift, scoff, believe, version, pious, spooked, oldtell, scholar, hometale.
# A reply with no m7 gets the plain closes. Mourning answers hand to keeping.sorry (k=grief).

# ================================================================ The weather: openers (talk.weather: outdoors only)

rule m7_wx_open_any
when concept=talk.weather
cooldown 1d
say Look at it. Just look at it. | What do you make of this sky? | Strange weather for the time of year#tag#. | I can't make my mind up about today. | Funny old sky today.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_rain
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=rain
cooldown 1d
say It's coming down in rods. | My hood's given up. | Another day of this #rain#. | I've had drier baths. | I can feel it in my boots. | It's found its way down my collar. All of it.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_snow
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=snow
cooldown 1d
say #snow.capitalize# up to my hocks already. | It's settling. That's the trouble, it's settling. | I can't feel my paw pads. | Everything's gone quiet under it. | Snowing again. Sideways, this time.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_fog
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=fog
cooldown 1d
say I just begged a post's pardon. | You can taste this #fog#. | Can't see the end of my own tail. | Every sound's coming from the wrong side. | My whiskers are dripping.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_storm
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=storm
cooldown 1d
say #oath#! Did you hear that one? Shook my teeth. | This #wind# wants the roofs off. | I counted three between the flash and the bang. | Something's come loose somewhere and it's banging like a drum. | Hold on to your hat.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_clear
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=clear here.time=dawn|day
cooldown 1d
say Not a cloud. I don't trust it. | Now that's a sky. | Sun on my back for once. | You can see for miles today. | Look at that. Blue as a jay.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_clear_night
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=clear here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 1d
say Not a cloud. The owls'll be busy. | Look at that sky. You could count them all, if you'd the nights to spare. | Clear as a bell. The cold's coming down already. | Light enough to find the way home without a lamp.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_overcast
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=overcast
cooldown 1d
say Grey as a pot lid. | It can't decide whether to rain. | The sky's sulking. | Heavy, isn't it? Like it's holding its breath. | No sun, no rain. Just grey.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_sandstorm
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=sandstorm
cooldown 1d
say I've dust in places dust shouldn't be. | Cover your eyes. | Can't see the field for the dirt in the air. | It's in my teeth. Grit, all of it.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_dawn_frost
when concept=talk.weather here.time=dawn here.season=winter|autumn here.weather=clear|overcast
cooldown 1d
say Frost on everything. The pump handle bit me. | White on the roofs this morning. | My breath's coming out in clouds. | The puddles have lids on.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_dusk_summer
when concept=talk.weather here.time=dusk here.season=summer here.weather=clear
cooldown 1d
say Warm evening. The ground's still giving off the day. | Swifts screaming overhead. | Light till all hours, this time of year. | Lovely, this. Don't tell anyone I said so.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_night_rain
when concept=talk.weather here.time=night here.weather=rain|storm
cooldown 1d
say Only fools and the watch out in this. | Black as a tar barrel, and wet with it. | I'll be dripping on the floor till morning. | Can't hear yourself think for it.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_spring_rain
when concept=talk.weather here.season=spring here.weather=rain|overcast
cooldown 1d
say Green rain. You can smell things growing. | The buds won't mind it. | Smells of earth and wet blossom. | Every ditch has a song in it today.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_summer_heat
when concept=talk.weather here.season=summer here.time=day here.weather=clear here.region!=frosthollow
cooldown 1d
say My tongue's out to my chin. | Too hot for fur. | The flies are the only ones enjoying this. | I've been panting since breakfast.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_autumn_wind
when concept=talk.weather here.season=autumn here.weather=overcast|storm|rain
cooldown 1d
say Leaves everywhere. In my collar, even. | The #wind#'s got a bite to it now. | Summer's packed up and gone without a word. | Smell that? Woodsmoke and wet leaves.
then other: moment.reply_weather

# Openers by who's speaking: their work, their home, their age.

rule m7_wx_open_farmer_dry
when concept=talk.weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=clear here.season=summer
cooldown 2d
say The ground's cracking. We want rain. | Lovely day if you're not a turnip. | Another dry one. The peas are curling up.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_farmer_wet
when concept=talk.weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=rain here.season=autumn
cooldown 2d
say Can't get the last of it in. Not in this. | The stooks are sodden. | Rain at harvest. Every year the same prayer, and the same answer.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_fisher
when concept=talk.weather self.job=fisher|sailor here.weather=storm|fog
cooldown 2d
say No boats out today. Not one. | I'd not take a rowboat across a puddle in this. | Somebody's out there in it. Somebody always is.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_guard
when concept=talk.weather self.job=guard|soldier here.weather=rain|snow|storm
cooldown 2d
say Eight hours in this, and the captain wants the boots polished. | My mail's rusting as I stand here. | Nobody causes trouble in weather like this. Small mercies.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_carter
when concept=talk.weather self.job=carter here.weather=rain|snow|storm
cooldown 2d
say The road'll be #mud# to the axles. | I've a load due by dusk and no hope of it. | Horses hate it. I hate it. We're agreed.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_old
when concept=talk.weather self.stage=old here.weather=rain|fog|overcast
cooldown 2d
say My knees told me yesterday. | Weather's not what it was. Wetter. | Seventy years under this sky, and I like it less every one.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_young
when concept=talk.weather self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Who makes the weather? | Why's the sky that colour? | Can clouds fall down? | Does the sky ever run out of weather?
then other: moment.reply_weather
remember pair: m7o=pup 2m

rule m7_wx_open_south_in_snow
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=snow self.from=oakhaven|mirebridge|larkfield|southmeadow
cooldown 2d
say Where I come from this is a story you tell pups. | I didn't know cold went this deep. | How do you live like this? Honestly. How?
then other: moment.reply_weather
remember pair: m7o=far 2m

rule m7_wx_open_north_in_heat
when concept=talk.weather here.region=south here.season=summer here.weather=clear self.from=frosthollow|coldwater
cooldown 2d
say Does the sun never go in, down here? | Is it always this hot down here? | My fur was made for snow, not this.
then other: moment.reply_weather
remember pair: m7o=far 2m

rule m7_wx_open_city_rain_away
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=rain here.region!=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere
cooldown 2d
say Ah. Rain. Almost feels like home. | You call this rain? In Ridgemere we'd call it a dry spell. | Smells like the Sound, this.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_poor_cold
when concept=talk.weather self.wealth=destitute|poor here.season=winter here.weather=snow|rain|overcast|storm self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
priority 1
say No wood till Restday. We sleep in our coats. | The damp's in the walls again. | Cold's dearer for some than others.
then other: moment.reply_weather
remember pair: m7o=need 2m

rule m7_wx_open_homeless
when concept=talk.weather self.homeless=yes here.weather=rain|snow|storm
cooldown 1d
priority 2
say Where'll I sleep tonight, in this? | Every doorway's taken. | I've been wet three days now. You stop noticing. Almost.
then other: moment.reply_weather
remember pair: m7o=need 2m

# ================================================================ The weather: answers (self is the one answering)

rule m7_wx_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_weather
say Could be worse. Could be raining frogs. | It'll change. It always does. | I've stopped looking up. Saves disappointment. | Weather's weather. You can't argue with it. | Mm. Same sky over all of us.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_any2
when concept=moment.reply_weather
say My mother said you can't eat weather, so stop chewing it. | It is what it is. | Keeps us talking, at least. | The sky doesn't ask our leave, does it?
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=rain
say Ducks are happy. Someone ought to be. | The water butt's full, so that's one thing. | Washes the fleas out, I suppose. | #annoyed#. Wet as a fish's elbow.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=moan 2m

rule m7_wx_re_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=snow
say It'll be grey slush by noon. | Pretty for an hour. Then it's just #cold#. | Mind the eaves. They drop it on you. | If a snowball finds you later, it wasn't me.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_fog
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=fog
say Keep to the path. | I heard the cart before I saw it. Nearly lost a tail. | Fog's good for one thing: nobody sees you yawn. | It'll lift. Or we'll all wander off and get lost.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_storm
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=storm
say Inside, and quick about it. | I've tied everything down that'll tie. | The gods are moving furniture. | That one was close. Too close.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=fear 2m

rule m7_wx_re_clear
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=clear here.time=dawn|day
say Make the most of it. That's #luck#, that is. | Washing day, then. | Don't say it out loud. You'll scare it off. | I'll take it. I'll take every scrap of it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=glad 2m

rule m7_wx_re_clear_night
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=clear here.time=dusk|night
say No cloud to keep the warmth in. It'll bite tonight. | Stars thick as frost. | Pretty. Cold, but pretty. | I'll want two blankets.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_overcast
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=overcast
say It'll rain before long. | It's thinking about it. | Grey's restful, if you let it be. | No shadows, at least. Can't see your own gloom.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_sandstorm
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=sandstorm
say Shut your mouth and walk. | It'll blow through. | Keep a wet cloth over your nose.
then other: moment.close

# By their work.

rule m7_wx_re_farmer_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer
cooldown 1d
say Don't curse it. That's bread falling. | My fields have been begging for this. | Every drop's a loaf in the autumn.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=glad 2m

rule m7_wx_re_farmer_harvest_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=rain|storm here.season=autumn
cooldown 1d
say Half my barley's still standing out in it. | It'll sprout in the stook if it keeps on. | I've stopped looking at the sky. It only laughs.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_farmer_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=snow
cooldown 1d
say I was up before light digging the ewes out. | Snow's a blanket for the winter wheat. | The beasts want feeding whatever falls.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_fisher_fog
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=fisher|sailor here.weather=fog
cooldown 1d
say No boat goes out in this. Not if they want to come back. | Fog on the water's the worst. You row in circles. | I've lost the shore in fog once. Never again.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=boats 2m

rule m7_wx_re_fisher_storm
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=fisher|sailor here.weather=storm|rain
cooldown 1d
say I've doubled the lines on the boat. | The water's white out there. Nobody's fool enough. | Wind's the killer, not the wet.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=boats 2m

rule m7_wx_re_fisher_clear
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=fisher|sailor here.weather=clear
cooldown 1d
say Flat water. Good for the nets. | Clear sky, cold night. Fish go deep. | I should be out. Why am I talking to you?
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_guard
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=guard|soldier here.weather=rain|snow|storm|fog
cooldown 1d
say I'm on the wall in it tonight. Lucky me. | Thieves stay in when it's like this. So should I. | My cloak's been wet since Dawnday.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_carter
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=carter here.weather=rain|snow|storm
cooldown 1d
say The roads'll be ruined. Three days late, everything. | My wheels will be #mud# to the hub. | I've a horse with a cough and a load of slate. Wish me luck.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_carter_fog
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=carter here.weather=fog
cooldown 1d
say I'll walk at the horse's head all the way, in this. | Last fog I drove the cart into a hedge. The hedge won. | Can't see the ruts. I'll feel for them.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_miner
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=miner
cooldown 1d
say I'll be under the hill soon. It's always the same weather down there. | Sun, snow, it's all one in the dark. | Lucky you, to care what the sky does.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_smith_cold
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=smith here.season=winter
cooldown 1d
say Come and stand by my forge. Warmest spot in town. | I've the only warm paws for a mile. | Everyone's my friend in winter. Funny, that.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_smith_heat
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=smith|baker|cook here.season=summer here.weather=clear here.region!=frosthollow
cooldown 1d
say Try a day by the fire in this. | I've been baking along with the bread. | I'd trade you for the shade.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_innkeeper_wet
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=innkeeper|brewer here.weather=rain|snow|storm
cooldown 1d
say Good for trade. Wet wolves want a fire and a jar. | I shouldn't say it, but I love a wet night. Full house. | Keep it coming, I say. My taproom thanks it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_merchant_wet
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.role=merchant here.weather=rain|storm|snow
cooldown 1d
say Nobody buys when they're wet. | My awning's a waterfall. | I've sold one thing all day, and that was a hood.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=moan 2m

rule m7_wx_re_healer_winter
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=healer here.season=winter|autumn
cooldown 1d
say Every chest in town's rattling. I'm run off my paws. | Wrap up. I've no room for one more cough. | Cold brings me trade I'd rather not have.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_priest
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=priest
cooldown 1d
say We take what's sent, and give thanks for a roof. | The Bright One sends weather on the deserving and the rest alike. | Weather keeps us humble.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_woodcutter_storm
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=woodcutter here.weather=storm
cooldown 1d
say I'll be clearing windfall for a week. | Trees down everywhere tomorrow, you watch. | Never stand under an old tree in a #wind# like this.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_laborer_heat
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=laborer|miner|woodcutter here.season=summer here.weather=clear here.time=day here.region!=frosthollow
cooldown 1d
say I've hauled sacks since dawn in it. My tongue's dragging. | Try carrying stone in this. | Water. I need water and a cellar.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_wx_re_beggar
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=beggar here.weather=rain|snow|storm
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say Easy for some to talk about it. | Spare a copper for a dry crust? | I'll be under the bridge again tonight.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=poor 2m

# By their home: the weather as it falls on one from elsewhere.

rule m7_wx_re_south_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=snow self.from=oakhaven|mirebridge|larkfield|southmeadow
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Back home we'd be mending fences in our shirtsleeves. | At home I'd only seen snow on the far hills. Now it's in my boots. | I keep thinking it'll stop. It never stops.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_wx_re_south_cold
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.season=winter here.region=north self.from=southmeadow|larkfield|oakhaven
cooldown 1d
say Winter down south is a brisk autumn up here. | I've worn every coat I own. At once. | My blood's too thin for the north. Always was.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_wx_re_north_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=snow self.from=frosthollow
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Call this snow? Up the valley it's to the eaves. | This is a dusting. Come back when you can't find the door. | Snow's a friend if you know it. Treat it right.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_north_heat
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.season=summer here.weather=clear self.from=frosthollow|coldwater here.region!=frosthollow|coldwater
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Up home there'd still be snow in the gullies. I'd give a week's wage to roll in it. | I'm cooking in my own fur. | Glasswater would be cold enough to stop your heart right now. Lovely.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_wx_re_fen_fog
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=fog self.from=mirebridge
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say This? In the fens this is a clear morning. | Fog's only air with something to say. | You learn to walk by smell in Mirebridge.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_city_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=rain self.from=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say I'm Ridgemere born. Rain's just air you can see. | In Ridgemere we don't call it rain unless it's sideways. | Rain doesn't count till it's coming up off the cobbles.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_lake_clear
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=clear|overcast self.from=coldwater here.region!=coldwater|ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say On a day like this Glasswater goes still as a plate. I miss it. | Nothing here to look into. At home you'd see your face in the lake. | I keep looking for the water and finding walls.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_wx_re_downs_wind
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=overcast|storm self.from=larkfield here.region!=larkfield
cooldown 1d
say On the downs you'd feel this wind coming a day off. | I miss a good wind across open grass. Here it just whistles round corners. | Larks'd be up in this at home, singing into it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_wx_re_wood_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=rain self.from=oakhaven here.region!=oakhaven
cooldown 1d
say Under the Warmwood you'd barely feel it. The leaves take it all. | Rain's nicer with a roof of oak over you. | I miss the smell of wet leaf mould. Sounds daft.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

# By age, means and mood.

rule m7_wx_re_old_bones
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.stage=old here.weather=rain|fog|snow|overcast
cooldown 1d
say My hip told me this a day ago. Hip's never wrong. | I've seen worse. I've seen the winter the wells froze solid. | At my age you're grateful for any weather you wake up to.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_young_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.stage=young here.weather=snow
cooldown 1d
say Can we build a snow fort? A big one? | I ate some. It tastes of nothing. | I'm going to slide down the lane on my tail!
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=glad 2m

rule m7_wx_re_young_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.stage=young here.weather=rain|storm
cooldown 1d
say Puddles! The big one by the well's up to my knees! | Is the thunder angry at us? | I'm not cold. I'm not. My teeth just do that.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_adolescent
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.stage=adolescent
cooldown 1d
say Who cares? It's weather. | Can we not talk about the weather? Please? | Everyone always talks about the weather. Every single day.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_poor
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.wealth=destitute|poor here.weather=rain|snow|storm here.season=autumn|winter self.stage=adult|old
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say The roof's leaking over the bed again. | I can't buy wood and bread both this week. | We'll huddle. We always huddle.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=poor 2m

rule m7_wx_re_rich
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.wealth=rich here.weather=rain|snow|storm self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 1d
say I've had the fires lit in every room. | The carriage leaks, if you can believe it. | Tiresome. I'll stay in and read.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=posh 2m

rule m7_wx_re_tired
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.tired=yes
cooldown 1d
say I'm too #tired# to mind what the sky does. | Rain, shine, I'll sleep through it given half a chance. | Don't care. I want #bed#.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=weary 2m

rule m7_wx_re_mourning
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.mourning=kin|friend
priority 2
cooldown 1d
say I hadn't noticed. I don't notice much this week. | They'd have had something to say about it. They always did. | Is it? I've not looked up in days.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule m7_wx_re_dry
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.humour=dry self.stage!=young
cooldown 1d
say Remarkable. Weather, happening, outdoors. | Next you'll tell me it's dark at night. | I'll write to the Council. They'll sort it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_merry_wet
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.humour=merry here.weather=rain|storm|snow|fog
cooldown 1d
say Lovely day for a duck! Or a fish. Or a wet wolf. | I've given up being dry. It's very freeing. | Sky's having a worse day than us, and that's saying something.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_merry_fair
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.humour=merry here.weather=clear|overcast
cooldown 1d
say I'd sing, but I'd frighten the birds. | Weather like this, I could dance. Don't hold me to it. | Grand. Somebody fetch the cider.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_wx_re_short
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.temper=short
cooldown 1d
say Talking about it won't change it. | #agree#, I can see it. I've got eyes. | And?
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_quiet
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.talk=quiet
cooldown 1d
say Mm. | Aye. | It is.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_devout
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.piety=devout here.weather=storm|snow|rain
cooldown 1d
say I'll light a candle for the ones out in it. | Pray for the boats and the shepherds. | It's sent. We bear it.
then other: moment.close

# A pup's question about the sky (m7o=pup).

rule m7_wx_re_to_pup
when concept=moment.reply_weather pair.mem.m7o=pup self.stage=adult|old
priority 3
say Ask a shepherd. They talk to it all day. | The Bright One sends it. Don't ask me why. | Because it can, pup. Same as you. | Never yet, and I've been watching a long while.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=topup 2m

rule m7_wx_re_to_pup_merry
when concept=moment.reply_weather pair.mem.m7o=pup self.stage=adult|old self.humour=merry|dry
priority 3
say There's a wolf on the hill with a great bellows. Blows it all our way. | Somebody up there's washing their blankets. | Ask the clouds. They never tell me anything.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=topup 2m

rule m7_wx_re_pup_pup
when concept=moment.reply_weather pair.mem.m7o=pup self.stage=young|adolescent
priority 3
say Dunno. Ask a grown-up. | My brother says the sky's a big lake upside down. | From the mountains. Everything bad comes from the mountains.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=pupchat 2m

# ================================================================ Answering the opener's own plight (any of the moment's
# answers): in need (m7o=need), far from home (m7o=far), working while others rest (m7o=busy). Priority 3, so the
# answer meets what was said.

rule m7_re_need
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=need
priority 3
say #bad.capitalize# times. Harder for some. | The chapel gives out bread on Restday. Go early. | I'm sorry. I truly am. | It won't always be like this. It can't be.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=sorry 2m

rule m7_re_need_warm
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=need self.warmth=warm self.wealth!=destitute|poor self.stage=adult|old
priority 3
say Come to ours tonight. There's a fire and a pot, and room for you. | Here. Don't argue. Take it. | You'll eat with us. That's settled. Bring whoever's yours.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=offer 2m

rule m7_re_need_rich
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=need self.wealth=rich self.stage=adult|old
priority 3
say Here. For wood. No, I insist. | Take this. Buy something hot. | I'll have something sent round. See that it is.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=offer 2m

rule m7_re_need_poor
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=need self.wealth=destitute|poor
priority 3
say Same boat, you and me. Leaking the same. | We'll share what there is. Which is nothing, twice. | Don't I know it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=same 2m

rule m7_re_need_cold
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=need self.warmth=cold self.stage=adult|old
priority 3
say Should've put some by. | Everyone's got troubles. | Work harder, then.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=snub 2m

rule m7_re_need_pup
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=need self.stage=young
priority 3
say You can have half my bread. Here. | My mum'll let you sit by our fire. Probably. | I've got a penny. You can have it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=pupgift 2m

rule m7_re_far
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=far
priority 3
say You'll get used to it. Everyone does. | Give it a year. It'll be home before you know it. | Miss it, do you? | Bit different from home, eh?
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=farre 2m

rule m7_re_far_same
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=far pair.same_from=yes
priority 3
say Don't. I'll start missing it too. | I know. I think of it every day. | One day we'll both go back. You'll see.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=together 2m

rule m7_re_far_local
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=far self.from=frosthollow|coldwater here.region=frosthollow|coldwater here.weather=snow
priority 3
say Soft. You're soft. You'll harden up. | This is mild. Wait till midwinter. | Wrap up and stop whining. We'll make a mountain wolf of you.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=tease 2m

rule m7_re_busy
when concept=moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival|moment.reply_weather pair.mem.m7o=busy
priority 3
say Somebody has to, I suppose. | Don't let them work you into the ground. | Shall I bring you something? A pie? | You'll rest when it's done.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=busy 2m

# ================================================================ Closing (self is the one who began), by how it went

rule m7_close_any
when concept=moment.close
say Well. There it is. | #farewell#. | Ah well. | I'll let you get on. | So it goes.
weight 1.5

rule m7_close_any2
when concept=moment.close
say #saying#. | True enough. | Can't argue with that. | Mm. Well, then.

rule m7_close_dry
when concept=moment.close self.humour=dry !pair.mem.m7
say Riveting. | We should do this more often. Or less. | Well, that's the day's excitement. | I'll treasure this talk.

rule m7_close_quiet
when concept=moment.close self.talk=quiet !pair.mem.m7
say Mm. | Aye. | ...Aye. | Mm. Right.

rule m7_close_moan
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=moan
priority 1
say Chin up. It can't last for ever. | It'll pass. Most things do. | Aye, well. We'll live.

rule m7_close_moan_warm
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=moan self.warmth=warm
priority 1
say Come by mine later. There's a fire and a pot on. | Tomorrow'll be better. I'll see that it is. | Cheer up, #address#. I'll stand you something hot.

rule m7_close_glad
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=glad
priority 1
say That's the spirit. | Ha. You've cheered me up. | Let's have more days like this, then.

rule m7_close_joke
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=joke
priority 1
say Ha! | Get away with you. | You're no help at all. | I walked into that one.

rule m7_close_work
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=work
priority 1
say Rather you than me. | Don't let it grind you down. | #oath#, and I thought I had it bad.

rule m7_close_work_adult
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=work self.stage=adult|old
priority 1
say Rather you than me. | Don't let it grind you down. | I'll stand you #drink# when it's done. | #oath#, and I thought I had it bad.

rule m7_close_fear
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=fear
priority 1
say Stay safe. | Get indoors, then. Both of us. | Mind the slates going home.

rule m7_close_boats
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=boats
priority 1
say Bright One keep them that are out on it. | Stay ashore, then. | I'll not go near the water today.

rule m7_close_crowd
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=crowd
priority 1
say Go on, then. I'll find you after. | Stick by me. I'll get us through. | Breathe. It thins out by the well.

rule m7_close_gossip
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=gossip
priority 1
say Go on, then. Who? | Tell me at the well. I've a pot on. | Save it. I'll want all of it later.

rule m7_close_weary
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=weary
priority 1
say Get to your bed, then. | Go on home. Sleep. | You look it, if you don't mind my saying.

rule m7_close_hungry
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=hungry
priority 1
say Go and eat, for pity's sake. | Then go and find a pie. | I can hear it from here.

rule m7_close_posh
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=posh
priority 1
say Well. I'm sure you'll manage. | Hard lives, some of us. | Mm. Terrible for you.

rule m7_close_posh_poor
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=posh self.wealth=destitute|poor
priority 1
say My heart bleeds. | We should all have your troubles. | A leaky carriage. Gods help us.

rule m7_close_posh_rich
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=posh self.wealth=rich
priority 1
say I know. One suffers. | Quite. Quite. | Ours has been the same. Dreadful.

rule m7_close_poor
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=poor
priority 1
say That's hard. I'm sorry. | It'll mend. Things do. | Hard times, these.

rule m7_close_poor_warm
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=poor self.warmth=warm self.wealth!=destitute|poor
priority 1
say Come by ours. There's always a bowl. | Here. Take this, and no arguing. | Don't you sleep out tonight. You hear me?

rule m7_close_poor_poor
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=poor self.wealth=destitute|poor
priority 1
say Two leaky boats, then. | We'll keep each other afloat. | Ha. Misery loves company.

rule m7_close_poor_cold
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=poor self.warmth=cold
priority 1
say Hm. Well. | Hard times all round. | The chapel takes folk in, I hear.

rule m7_close_poor_rich
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=poor self.wealth=rich
priority 1
say The chapel does good work, I'm told. | Ah. Well. One hears it's dreadful. | I'll mention it to someone.

rule m7_close_offer
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=offer
priority 2
say I... #thanks#. Truly. | Bless you. I'll not forget it. | You're too good. I'll pay you back. Somehow.

rule m7_close_pupgift
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=pupgift
priority 2
say Keep your bread, little one. But bless you for it. | You're a good pup. Your mother raised you right. | Ha. I'll hold you to that.

rule m7_close_same
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=same
priority 2
say Two leaky boats, then. | We'll keep each other afloat. | Ha. Misery loves company.

rule m7_close_sorry
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=sorry
priority 2
say Aye. Well. | Kind of you to say. | We'll manage. We always do.

rule m7_close_snub
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=snub
priority 2
say #annoyed#. Thanks for nothing. | I'll remember that. | Easy for you to say.

rule m7_close_farre
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=farre
priority 2
say So they keep telling me. | I hope you're right. | Some days more than others.

rule m7_close_together
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=together
priority 2
say One day. | Till then, there's two of us. | Aye. Together.

rule m7_close_tease
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=tease
priority 2
say I'll never be a mountain wolf. | Harden up yourself. | Gods help me.

rule m7_close_busy
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=busy
priority 2
say Aye. Back to it. | Don't tempt me to stop. | It won't do itself, more's the pity.

rule m7_close_home
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=home
priority 1
say Long way from home, then. | Tell me about it some time. Properly. | I'd like to see it one day. | You're here now, any road.

rule m7_close_home_cold
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=home self.warmth=cold
priority 1
say Nobody made you come. | Go back, then. | Everyone's from somewhere.

rule m7_close_local
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=local
priority 1
say So it's me that talks funny. Fair enough. | I'll pick it up. Give me a year. | Then I'd best mind my own voice.

rule m7_close_prickly
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=prickly
priority 1
say No offence meant. | Touchy. | Suit yourself.

rule m7_close_gladgone
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=gladgone
priority 1
say Can't blame you. | Their loss, then. | Ha. Fair enough.

rule m7_close_topup
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=topup
priority 2
say I'm going to ask my mum. | That's not what Brindle says. | Promise? | I knew it!

rule m7_close_pupchat
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=pupchat
priority 2
say You're making it up. | I'm telling everyone. | Race you to the corner!

rule m7_close_market
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=market
priority 1
say Ha. Mind your purse. | I'll look out for you in the crush. | Save me a pie if you get there first.

rule m7_close_rest
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=rest
priority 1
say Wise words. | Ha. Right you are. | Don't remind me.

rule m7_close_dawn
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=dawn
priority 1
say I'll leave you to wake up, then. | Go on. Off you go. | Same here, if I'm honest.

rule m7_close_night
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=night
priority 1
say Ha. Same as you, then. | Mind the watch doesn't take you for a thief. | Well. Don't stay out too late.

rule m7_close_done
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=done
priority 1
say That's the plan. | I will. Don't work too hard. | Home, and nothing till morning.

rule m7_close_both
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=both
priority 1
say Come on, then. First round's mine. | Aye. Let's sit a while. | Not a word about work. Agreed.

rule m7_close_dayoff
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=dayoff
priority 1
say I'll try. It doesn't come natural. | Lucky? I'll be bored by noon. | I mean to.

rule m7_close_teen
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=teen
priority 1
say Ha. I remember being your age. | Go on, then. Enjoy it. | Mind your manners, mind.

# Lore closes (the one who told the tale).

rule m7_close_scoff
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=scoff
priority 1
say Laugh all you like. | Believe what you want. My grandmother did. | Well, that's how I heard it. | You'll see. One of these nights.

rule m7_close_believe
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=believe
priority 1
say Keep a lamp lit tonight, then. | See? It's not just me. | Sleep well. Ha.

rule m7_close_version
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=version
priority 1
say Every hearth tells it its own way. | Yours sounds worse. I'll keep mine. | Tell me yours some night. With the lamp low.

rule m7_close_pious
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=pious
priority 1
say No harm in a tale. | Aye, well. It's still a good tale. | I'll say a prayer as well, then. To be safe.

rule m7_close_spooked
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=spooked
priority 1
say It's only a tale! Come back! | I'll walk you to your door, if you like. | Ha! Sleep with a lamp lit, then.

rule m7_close_oldtell
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=oldtell
priority 1
say Go on, then. I've time. | Another night. I'll bring the ale. | I'll hold you to that.

rule m7_close_scholar
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=scholar
priority 1
say You've no romance in you. | Smaller and duller. That's learning for you. | Read it me some time, then.

rule m7_close_hometale
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=hometale
priority 1
say Every place has its own way of telling it. | I'd like to hear your way some night. | Same tale, different mud.

rule m7_close_tale_devout
when concept=moment.close pair.mem.m7=scoff|believe|version|hometale self.piety=devout
priority 1
say The Bright One keeps us, tales or no. | I'll light a candle tonight all the same. | Tales are tales. Prayers are better.

# ================================================================ The day: openers (talk.day: two who know each other)

rule m7_day_open_any
when concept=talk.day
cooldown 1d
say Where's the day gone? | Feels like a long one already. | Is it only #here.weekday#? | Funny sort of day#tag#. | Days are getting away from me.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_market
when concept=talk.day here.day=market
cooldown 1d
say Marketday. The whole town's out with its purse. | Have you been round the stalls yet? | I've been elbowed three times and I've bought nothing. | Market crowd's thick as porridge today.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=market 2m

rule m7_day_open_rest
when concept=talk.day here.day=rest
cooldown 1d
say Restday at last. My paws thank the gods. | Quiet, isn't it? You can hear the birds. | I don't know what to do with myself on a Restday. | Nothing to do but sit. Lovely.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=rest 2m

rule m7_day_open_work
when concept=talk.day here.day=work here.time=dawn
cooldown 1d
say Up with the birds again. | Another day, another sack. | #here.weekday.capitalize#, and already I'm counting to Restday.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=dawn 2m

rule m7_day_open_dusk
when concept=talk.day here.time=dusk
cooldown 1d
say Lamps going on. Day's done. | That's the light gone. | Home, supper, #bed#. In that order. | Long shadows. My favourite hour.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=dusk 2m

rule m7_day_open_night
when concept=talk.day here.time=night
cooldown 1d
say What are you doing out at this hour? | You're up late. | Can't sleep either? | Late to be wandering, isn't it?
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=night 2m

rule m7_day_open_crowd
when concept=talk.day here.crowd=crowd
cooldown 1d
say Where's everyone come from? | Can't swing a cat for wolves today. | Mind your purse in this crush.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=crowd 2m

rule m7_day_open_quiet
when concept=talk.day here.crowd=quiet here.place=street|market
cooldown 1d
say Dead quiet. Where is everybody? | Just you and me and the pigeons. | Quiet as a chapel out here.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=quiet 2m

rule m7_day_open_rest_working
when concept=talk.day here.day=rest self.working=yes
cooldown 2d
say Restday, they call it. Not for me. | Somebody has to work while the rest of you pray. | I'll rest when I'm dead. Or Hearthday.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=busy 2m

rule m7_day_open_market_merchant
when concept=talk.day here.day=market self.role=merchant
cooldown 2d
say Good day for it. I've sold out of half the stall. | They're haggling like it's a sport. | Marketday's the only day that pays the rent.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=stall 2m

rule m7_day_open_after_shift
when concept=talk.day self.shift=after
cooldown 1d
say That's me done. Done, done, done. | Off my feet, finally. | Day's work's behind me. Don't mention it.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=done 2m

rule m7_day_open_day_off
when concept=talk.day self.shift=day_off
cooldown 1d
say Day off. I keep thinking I've forgotten something. | Nothing to do and all day to do it. | I slept till the bells. Shameless.
then other: moment.reply_day
remember pair: m7o=dayoff 2m

# ================================================================ The day: answers (self is the one answering)

# To a remark on the day as such (no m7o).

rule m7_day_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_day
say Same as ever. One foot, then the other. | I've stopped counting them. | Another day closer to something. | Aye. There's always tomorrow. | Days are like beans. All the same till you need one.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_any2
when concept=moment.reply_day
say Can't complain. Well, I can. | Mustn't grumble, so I won't. Much. | It's had its moments. | So far, so ordinary.
then other: moment.close

# To the opener's kind of day (priority 1).

rule m7_day_re_market
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=market
priority 1
say Once round. The prices'd make you weep. | I'm keeping my purse in my teeth. | I'm only here for the cheese. | Thick as porridge, and twice as slow.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=market 2m

rule m7_day_re_market_merchant
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=market self.role=merchant
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I've not sat down since dawn. Don't keep me. | Busy's good. Busy's rent. | One more haggler and I'll give it away to be rid of them.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_day_re_market_poor
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=market self.wealth=destitute|poor self.stage=adult|old
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I look. Looking's free. | Smelled the pies. That'll do me. | I've a penny and a list as long as my tail.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=poor 2m

rule m7_day_re_market_young
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=market self.stage=young
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say There's a wolf with a dancing bird! A real one! | I'm allowed one honey cake. Just one. | I lost my mother twice already.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=glad 2m

rule m7_day_re_stall
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=stall
priority 1
say Then you can stand me a pie. | Good. Your prices can come down, then. | Glad somebody's doing well out of it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_day_re_stall_merchant
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=stall self.role=merchant
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Lucky you. Mine's been dead as a doornail. | Same here. My voice is gone from crying my wares. | Don't boast. It brings the tax-farmers.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_rest
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=rest
priority 1
say Rest while you can. | I've done nothing all morning, and I'm proud of it. | Sit. That's the whole trick of it. | It won't last. Dawnday's coming.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=rest 2m

rule m7_day_re_rest_devout
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=rest self.piety=devout
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I've been to chapel twice. I'll go again at dusk. | Rest's a gift. You should take it. | A good sermon this morning. You missed it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=rest 2m

rule m7_day_re_rest_working
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=rest self.working=yes
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Easy for you. I've been at it since dawn. | Restday's for those who can afford it. | Someone has to keep the fires in.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_day_re_rest_restless
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=rest self.drive=restless|ambitious
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I hate Restdays. Nothing gets done. | I've tidied the house twice. | Tomorrow can't come soon enough.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_day_re_dawn
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=dawn
priority 1
say Birds have the right idea. They sing about it. | Don't. I've not woken up yet. | Ask me after I've eaten. | Same sack, different day.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=dawn 2m

rule m7_day_re_dusk
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=dusk
priority 1
say And not before time. | Supper and my own chair. I can taste it. | Best hour of the day, this. | Another one done, and nothing broken.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_dusk_old
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=dusk self.stage=old
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say At my age you're glad of every one. | Days go quicker the fewer you've got. | I watched the sun down. I always do.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_night
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=night
priority 1
say Couldn't sleep. | Walking it off. | I could ask you the same. | Better out here than staring at the rafters.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=night 2m

rule m7_day_re_night_young
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=night self.stage=young|adolescent
priority 1
say Don't tell my mum. | I'm going home. I'm going right now. | I heard a noise and came to look.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_day_re_crowd
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=crowd
priority 1
say Every village for a day's walk, by the look of it. | Keep your tail tucked in. | I've been trodden on twice.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=market 2m

rule m7_day_re_crowd_nervy
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=crowd self.temper=nervy
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Too many. Far too many. I can't breathe. | Everyone's treading on my tail. | I'm going home. I'll come back when it thins.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=crowd 2m

rule m7_day_re_quiet
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=quiet
priority 1
say Indoors, with any sense. | Suits me. | Don't complain. You'll bring the crowds. | Gone to the next town, I expect. Something's always better there.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_done
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=done
priority 1
say Off home with you, then. | Lucky. I've half a day yet. | Put your feet up. You've earned it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=done 2m

rule m7_day_re_done_too
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=done self.shift=after
priority 1
say Me too. Shall we find a bench? | Same. My back's made of wood. | Done and dusted. Let's not talk about it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=both 2m

rule m7_day_re_dayoff
when concept=moment.reply_day pair.mem.m7o=dayoff
priority 1
say Enjoy it. Don't waste it on the likes of me. | Make the most of it. | Lucky beast. | You'll have forgotten nothing. That's the feeling of rest.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=dayoff 2m

# As they are, whatever the opener (priority 1, so they stand with the keyed answers).

rule m7_day_re_guard
when concept=moment.reply_day self.on_watch=yes
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Can't stop. I'm on watch. | Long one. Ask me at the end of it. | Quiet so far. Don't say it. You'll jinx it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_day_re_tired
when concept=moment.reply_day self.tired=yes
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I'm that #tired# I could sleep on a fence. | I could sleep standing, like a horse. | Don't ask. I'll cry.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=weary 2m

rule m7_day_re_hungry
when concept=moment.reply_day self.hungry=yes
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I'll tell you after I've eaten. | I'm #hungry#. That's my whole day. | My belly's been talking louder than me.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=hungry 2m

rule m7_day_re_chatty
when concept=moment.reply_day self.talk=chatty
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Never mind that. You'll never guess who I saw at the well. | Oh, that reminds me. Have you heard about the baker's cart? | Listen, I've news. Sit down a moment.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=gossip 2m

rule m7_day_re_rich
when concept=moment.reply_day self.wealth=rich self.stage=adult|old !pair.mem.m7o
cooldown 2d
say Pleasant enough. Calls and letters. | A dull dinner, and a duller visit after it. | One does what one must.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=posh 2m

rule m7_day_re_mourning
when concept=moment.reply_day self.mourning=kin|friend
priority 2
cooldown 1d
say I get through them. That's all. | Every day's long, this week. | I keep thinking I'll tell them about it.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

# ================================================================ Festivals: openers (here.festival is the festival's
# name, today's or the one coming)

rule m7_fest_open_today
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.festival
cooldown 1d
say #greet#, and a happy #here.festival#! | #here.festival.capitalize# at last. | You've a ribbon on, I see. Proper #here.festival# spirit. | Smell that? That's a feast cooking.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_soon
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=soon here.festival
cooldown 1d
say #here.festival.capitalize#'s nearly on us. | Ready for #here.festival#? | Not long now till #here.festival#. | They've asked me to bring a pie for #here.festival#. Me! I burn water.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_today_spring
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.season=spring
cooldown 1d
say Blossom in every doorway. | They've hung green boughs over the gate. | First feast after the lean months. My belly cheered.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_today_summer
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.season=summer
cooldown 1d
say They'll dance till the light goes, and it goes late. | The fires'll be lit at dusk. | Too hot to dance. They'll dance anyway.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_today_autumn
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.season=autumn
cooldown 1d
say The last of it's in. Now we eat it. | Corn dollies on every door. | Bread, cider, more bread. That's the plan.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_today_winter
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.season=winter
cooldown 1d
say Dark early, and every window lit. | Look at it. Candles in every house. | The cold can't get in tonight. Not with all those fires.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_soon_poor
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=soon self.wealth=destitute|poor self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
priority 1
say How's a body to feast on nothing? | Everyone in new ribbons, and me in last year's coat. | Festivals are for those with full purses.
then other: moment.reply_festival
remember pair: m7o=need 2m

rule m7_fest_open_soon_cook
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=soon self.job=cook|baker|innkeeper|brewer
cooldown 2d
say I'll be baking from tonight till it's over. | Three days' work for one day's feast. | Order your pies now or go without.
then other: moment.reply_festival
remember pair: m7o=busy 2m

rule m7_fest_open_young_today
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Is it the feast now? Is it? | Will there be honey cakes? Say there will. | I'm going to stay up till the end. All of it.
then other: moment.reply_festival
remember pair: m7o=pup 2m

rule m7_fest_open_young_soon
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=soon self.stage=young here.festival
cooldown 1d
say How many sleeps till #here.festival#? | Will there be honey cakes? Say there will. | Is it #here.festival# tomorrow? Is it?
then other: moment.reply_festival
remember pair: m7o=pup 2m

# ================================================================ Festivals: answers

rule m7_fest_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_festival
say Wouldn't miss it for all the #money# in Ridgemere. | I've my good coat brushed and ready. | Aye. Eat, dance, regret it in the morning. | It comes round quicker every year. | I'll be there. Somewhere near the food.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=glad 2m

rule m7_fest_re_any2
when concept=moment.reply_festival
say Same as every year, and I'll love it the same. | Gods, the noise there'll be. | They'd better not run out of cider like last time.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_priest
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.job=priest
cooldown 1d
say Remember why we keep it, between the cups. | I've the blessing to say. Pray they listen. | The chapel first, then the feast. That's the order.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_guard
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.job=guard|soldier
cooldown 1d
say I'm on duty. Somebody's got to fish the drunks out of the trough. | Double watch. Every festival, the same fights. | I'll hear it from the wall. Lovely.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_fest_re_cook
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.job=cook|baker|innkeeper|brewer
cooldown 1d
say I'll be feeding the lot of you. Don't expect me to dance. | Every oven in town's going. | I've not seen my bed since yesterday.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=work 2m

rule m7_fest_re_merchant
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.role=merchant
cooldown 1d
say Best trade of the season. Ribbons sell themselves. | I've laid in triple stock. Pray I sell it. | Festivals are good to merchants. Very good.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_poor
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.wealth=destitute|poor self.stage=adult|old
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I'll watch. Watching's free. | The chapel feeds folk at festival. I'll be in the line. | Not this year. Maybe next.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=poor 2m

rule m7_fest_re_rich
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.wealth=rich self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 1d
say We'll give a little something to the town, of course. | I've a dinner to host. Twelve at table. Exhausting. | I've ordered more candles than the chapel.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=posh 2m

rule m7_fest_re_house
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.house self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say Our House always puts on a show. It's expected. | Father wants the whole hall lit. Every candle in the city. | The Council will be watching who gives most. As ever.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=posh 2m

rule m7_fest_re_mourning
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.mourning=kin|friend
priority 2
cooldown 1d
say I'll not go this year. | They loved this festival. I can't face it. | Maybe I'll sit at the back. Maybe.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule m7_fest_re_old
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.stage=old
cooldown 1d
say In my day it went three days, not one. | I've danced at sixty of them. I'll sit this one out. Maybe. | They don't sing the old songs any more. Nobody knows them.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_young
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say I'm going to eat six honey cakes. Six! | Can I stay up? Can I? | I've practised the dance. Watch! No, watch!
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=glad 2m

rule m7_fest_re_adolescent
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.stage=adolescent
cooldown 1d
say There's dancing after dark. Everyone's going. Everyone. | I'm not wearing that ribbon. I'm not. | Maybe someone'll ask me to dance. Maybe.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=teen 2m

rule m7_fest_re_from_away
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.from!=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 2d
say At home we do it different. More singing, less shoving. | It's not the same as at home. Bigger, but not the same. | Back home they'll be setting the long table about now.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_fest_re_short
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.temper=short
cooldown 1d
say Noise, drink and fools. I'll stay in. | Wake me when it's over. | Every year someone's sick on my step.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=joke 2m

rule m7_fest_re_devout
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.piety=devout
cooldown 1d
say I'll be at the chapel first. Give thanks before you feast. | It's a holy day before it's a drinking one. | I've a candle ready for the window.
then other: moment.close

# To a pup's festival questions (m7o=pup).

rule m7_fest_re_to_pup_today
when concept=moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=pup topic.when=today self.stage=adult|old
priority 3
say Cakes, and dancing, and a bonfire. If you're good. | Stay by your mother in the crowd, mind. | Till the end? We'll see who's asleep first. | It's today, you daft pup. Go and find the cakes.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=topup 2m

rule m7_fest_re_to_pup_soon
when concept=moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=pup topic.when=soon self.stage=adult|old
priority 3
say Not long. A few more sleeps. | Soon. Be good till then and there might be cakes. | Ask me again tomorrow, and the day after. Then it'll be here.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=topup 2m

rule m7_fest_re_pup_pup
when concept=moment.reply_festival pair.mem.m7o=pup self.stage=young|adolescent
priority 3
say I'm having two! | My big sister says there's a fire as high as a house. | I'm going to dance with everyone.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=pupchat 2m

# ================================================================ Lore: openers (talk.lore: the realm's tales, by anyone)

rule m7_lore_open_any
when concept=talk.lore
cooldown 1d
say My grandmother used to say the hills were sleeping giants. | They say a giant dragged one claw from Glasswater to the sea, and that's the Long River. | They say the old roads were laid by wolves who never slept. | Put your ear to the ground on a still night, they say, and you'll hear the dead talking.
then other: moment.reply_lore
remember pair: m7o=tale 2m

rule m7_lore_open_night
when concept=talk.lore here.time=night|dusk
cooldown 1d
say Don't whistle after dark. It calls things. | Count the stars and you'll go blind, my mother said. | They say a shiver at dusk means someone's stepped where you'll be buried. | Never answer a voice in the dark that knows your name.
then other: moment.reply_lore
remember pair: m7o=tale 2m

rule m7_lore_open_wardens
when concept=talk.lore
cooldown 2d
say Folk say the Wardens watch the Quickened from somewhere past the mountains. | Ever seen a Warden? My uncle swore he did. Grey cloak, no face. | If you've a gift, they say, the Wardens hear of it.
then other: moment.reply_lore
remember pair: m7o=tale 2m

rule m7_lore_open_houses
when concept=talk.lore here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 2d
say They say the first Greatly came ashore with a boat and a bag of salt. | They say the cellars under Grayrock Hall go down into the old mine and never stop. | They say there was a fifth House once, and the other four swore never to speak its name.
then other: moment.reply_lore
remember pair: m7o=tale 2m

rule m7_lore_open_old
when concept=talk.lore self.stage=old
cooldown 2d
say When I was a pup they said the winters were longer because the wolves were kinder. | My gran told me a comet came in her girlhood and burned the sky a week. | My father swore the old well spoke to him, the night before the flood.
then other: moment.reply_lore
remember pair: m7o=tale 2m

rule m7_lore_open_young
when concept=talk.lore self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Is it true there's a dragon under the hill? | Is there really a wolf with no shadow that walks the roads at night? | Do the dead come back on the longest night? Brindle says so.
then other: moment.reply_lore
remember pair: m7o=pup 2m

# ================================================================ Lore: answers (to a tale told, m7o=tale)

rule m7_lore_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_lore
say Every grandmother says that. | Who told you that? | Old tales have a grain of something in them. Not much.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=scoff 2m

rule m7_lore_re_any2
when concept=moment.reply_lore
say My mother told it the same. Word for word. | Don't. I'll never sleep. | Hush. Somebody'll hear. | That's nonsense, and I believe every word.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=believe 2m

rule m7_lore_re_any3
when concept=moment.reply_lore
say I heard it different. Worse, my version. | That's not how my gran told it. Hers had a fox in it. | You've left the best bit out.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=version 2m

rule m7_lore_re_frank
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.honesty=frank
cooldown 1d
say #nonsense.capitalize#. Pure #nonsense#. | Tales are for pups and drunks. | I'll believe it when it pays my rent.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=scoff 2m

rule m7_lore_re_devout
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.piety=devout
cooldown 1d
say The Bright One made the world. The rest is gossip. | Don't speak lightly of such things. | There's more under the sky than the priests tell us. I'll grant that.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=pious 2m

rule m7_lore_re_old
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.stage=old
cooldown 1d
say That's not how it goes. Sit down, I'll tell it right. | I knew a wolf who knew a wolf who was there. | They told it better when I was young. Slower.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=oldtell 2m

rule m7_lore_re_young
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Is that true? Truly true? | I'm not scared. I'm just going to stand behind you. | Tell it again! The scary bit!
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=believe 2m

rule m7_lore_re_scholar
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.job=scholar|priest|official
cooldown 1d
say There's something like it in the old rolls, if you can read the hand. | The records say something of the kind. Duller, mind. | Tales grow in the telling. The truth's usually smaller.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=scholar 2m

rule m7_lore_re_nervy
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.temper=nervy here.time=night|dusk
cooldown 1d
say Why would you say that? Now? Here? | I'm going home. Right now. With a lamp. | Did you hear that? Behind us?
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=spooked 2m

# From elsewhere: each country's way of telling it (never said at home, where everyone tells it so).

rule m7_lore_re_from_frost
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=frosthollow here.region!=frosthollow
cooldown 2d
say Up the valley they'd say it's the mountain breathing. Everything's the mountain, with us. | We've a tale like it. Ends with a cave-in. They all do. | In Frosthollow we'd knock on the mine door for luck before we said that aloud.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=hometale 2m

rule m7_lore_re_from_cold
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=coldwater here.region!=coldwater
cooldown 2d
say At Coldwater we'd say the lake knows. The lake knows everything. | My grandfather would throw a fish back for saying that. | There's a tale like it about Glasswater. Colder, mind.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=hometale 2m

rule m7_lore_re_from_oak
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=oakhaven here.region!=oakhaven
cooldown 2d
say In the Warmwood we'd say an oak saw it. Oaks see everything. | We tell that one round the fire at story night. Better, mind. | My granddam told it with a ghost in it. Always a ghost, in Oakhaven.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=hometale 2m

rule m7_lore_re_from_mire
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=mirebridge here.region!=mirebridge
cooldown 2d
say In the fens we'd say: don't follow the lights. That's the end of every tale. | Fen folk know a dozen like it, and every one's true. Mostly. | My aunt would spit three times and touch iron.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=hometale 2m

rule m7_lore_re_from_lark
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=larkfield here.region!=larkfield
cooldown 2d
say A carter told me that one at home. Taller, it was. | In Larkfield you'd pay a penny for a tale like that, and get change. | Every tale passes through Larkfield sooner or later. That one came back muddier.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=hometale 2m

rule m7_lore_re_from_south
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=southmeadow here.region!=southmeadow
cooldown 2d
say Down south we'd tell that at harvest, with the cider going round. | Every field in Southmeadow has its story. That's a field tale if ever I heard one. | We'd say a scarecrow saw it. Don't laugh.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=hometale 2m

rule m7_lore_re_from_city
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=ridgemere here.region!=ridgemere
cooldown 2d
say In the city they'd say it was a House that did it. It's always a House. | We've a tale like that in Ridgemere. Ends with somebody owing money. | City folk don't believe tales. We believe rumours. Different thing.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=hometale 2m

# To a pup's question (m7o=pup).

rule m7_lore_re_to_pup
when concept=moment.reply_lore pair.mem.m7o=pup self.stage=adult|old
priority 3
say Only for pups who stay up late. So don't. | Who's been filling your head? ...No. Probably not. | Ask your gran. She'll tell it scarier than me. | Not round here. The watch wouldn't stand for it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=topup 2m

rule m7_lore_re_to_pup_old
when concept=moment.reply_lore pair.mem.m7o=pup self.stage=old
priority 3
cooldown 1d
say Sit down, pup, and I'll tell you the whole of it. | When I was your size, we were told the same. And I'm still here. | There is. And it likes pups who don't do as they're told.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=topup 2m

rule m7_lore_re_pup_pup
when concept=moment.reply_lore pair.mem.m7o=pup self.stage=young|adolescent
priority 3
say Brindle says a lot of things. | I'm not scared. You're scared. | Let's go and look! ...Tomorrow. In the day.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=pupchat 2m

# ================================================================ Where you're from (talk.accent): b's voice noticed

rule m7_acc_open_any
when concept=talk.accent
cooldown 1d
say Where's that voice from? | I can't place your voice. Where's it from? | Say that again. I like how you say it. | #surprise#! There's a voice from somewhere.
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_rude
when concept=talk.accent self.warmth=cold
cooldown 2d
say Can't understand a word you say. | Talk properly, will you? | Where'd you learn to talk like that? A barn?
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_warm
when concept=talk.accent self.warmth=warm
cooldown 2d
say I love that voice. Where's it from? | You've a lovely way of talking. Like music. | Go on, say something else. I could listen all day.
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_young
when concept=talk.accent self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say Why do you talk funny? | Say something else! You talk like a story. | Are you from far away? Really far?
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_city
when concept=talk.accent here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere
cooldown 2d
say Fresh off the road, are you? | You'll lose that voice in a year. The city wears it off. | That's never a city voice. I can always tell.
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_merchant
when concept=talk.accent self.role=merchant
cooldown 2d
say A #topic.accent_town# voice! I had a carter from there once. Never paid me. | I'd know that voice in a crowd. Your folk come to my stall. | #topic.accent_town#, is it? I'll mind my weights, then.
then other: moment.reply_home

# Answers about home (self is the one whose voice was noticed; topic.accent_town is where they grew up). One answering
# where they stand at home (the one who asked is the stranger) answers that, first.

rule m7_home_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_home
say #topic.accent_town#, born and bred. | #topic.accent_town#, if you must know. | From #topic.accent_town#. It shows, does it? | #topic.accent_town#. I'll die talking like it.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_home_re_frost
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=frosthollow
priority 1
say Frosthollow. Up the Pass Road, under the Whitefangs. Where the snow lives. | The valley. Frosthollow. We say what we mean, and not much of it. | Miner's voice, that. Frosthollow. Grew up by lamplight.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_home_re_cold
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=coldwater
priority 1
say Coldwater. On Glasswater, under the mountains. You'd love it. Or freeze. | Lake country. We talk slow. The fish don't hurry, why should we? | Coldwater. I can still smell the reeds when I close my eyes.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_home_re_oak
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=oakhaven
priority 1
say Oakhaven. The Warmwood. Green all summer, and then some. | From under the oaks. We take our time, in Oakhaven. | The Warmwood, aye. Slow talk from a slow wood.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_home_re_mire
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=mirebridge
priority 1
say Mirebridge. The fens. Wet feet, and a wetter voice. | Fen-born. Sallow Fens, by the Long River. Wet feet and long memories. | Mirebridge. Don't make the face. Everyone makes the face.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

rule m7_home_re_lark
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=larkfield
priority 1
say Larkfield. The downs. I was raised shouting prices over sheep. | Larkfield. Every carter in the realm drinks in our inn. | The Larkdowns. Wide skies, quick tongues.
then other: moment.close
remember pair: m7=home 2m

